## Source taxonomy

Sources should be modeled by class.

## A. Crafting

Player crafts an item directly.

Properties:
- repeatable
- ingredient-dependent
- affected by crafting modifiers
- can create mastery through crafted output
- subject to crafting-specific overflow rules

Notes:
- resource saver applies here
- crafting overflow does not produce extra crafted-item mastery

---

## B. Manual exploring

Player explores directly using stamina.

Properties:
- stamina-based
- zone-dependent
- affected by explore stamina modifiers
- uses normal zone drop rates

---

## C. Apple Cider

Click-reduction explore source that performs many explores at once.

Properties:
- stamina-based
- zone-dependent
- affected by Exploring Effectiveness and cider-specific perks
- changes drop-rate behavior
- not automatically the most efficient strategy

Notes:
- should be modeled separately from manual exploring

---

## D. Lemonade

Fixed-yield instant-drop exploring consumable.

Properties:
- fixed yield
- no Exploring Effectiveness interaction
- perk-sensitive
- not stamina-based in the same way as manual/cider explore

---

## E. Arnold Palmer

Fixed-yield instant-drop exploring consumable crafted from Iced Tea + Lemonade.

Properties:
- fixed yield at use time
- crafted source at supply time
- no Exploring Effectiveness interaction
- affected by AP-specific perk/meal modifiers
- sits at the boundary between crafting and exploring

Notes:
- should be modeled both:
  - as a direct acquisition source when used
  - as a crafted object with recipe/resource cost

---

## F. Owned containers / owned stockpile items

Already-owned bags, chests, or similar sources that can yield items/mastery.

Examples:
- corn prize bags
- chests already owned

Properties:
- finite
- user-state dependent
- immediately usable
- not generally stamina-based

---

## G. Pet collection

Distinct source class with two subtypes:

### G1. Stored pet inventory
Items already accumulated and currently waiting to be collected.

Properties:
- finite
- immediately available
- user-state dependent
- practical early target for planning

### G2. Future pet production
Items that pets could still generate over time.

Properties:
- time-dependent
- renewable over time
- subject to seasonality and offline caps
- should be reported separately from stored pet inventory

---

## H. One-time rewards

Examples:
- Tower rewards
- one-time unlock rewards

Properties:
- not repeatable
- usually poor fit for practical planning
- excluded by default unless explicitly enabled later

---

## I. Impractical / excluded sources

Examples:
- Flea Market
- Exchange Center

Properties:
- technically possible
- not useful for practical planning
- excluded by default

---

## Default source policy

### Include by default
- crafting
- manual exploring
- Apple Cider
- Lemonade
- Arnold Palmer
- owned containers
- stored pet inventory

### Include later / separately
- simple future pet production estimates

### Exclude by default
- Flea Market
- Exchange Center
- one-time Tower rewards

Rationale:
The planner should model practical play, not every theoretical path.

