## Known confirmed rules and assumptions

## Crafting

- Resource Saver I = +10% crafted output
- Resource Saver II = +15% crafted output
- Resource Saver III = +20% crafted output
- Resource saver is additive across these sources
- planning interpretation is deterministic expected value
- example: +45% saver means 100 crafts yields 145 effective outputs

### Crafting overflow
- if crafting would exceed inventory max, blocked crafted output is not received
- resources are refunded
- blocked crafted output does not produce additional crafted-item mastery

---

## Mastery bonuses

- Mushroom Stew = +10% mastery for 5 minutes
- Mushroom Stew applies broadly to mastery
- event mastery bonuses may exist and are variable
- event resource saver bonuses may exist and are variable

---

## Manual exploring

### Wanderer
Known tiers:
- I = 4%
- II = 7%
- III = 9%
- IV = 13%

Planning interpretation:
- store both perk tiers and effective percent
- treat as expected-value stamina reduction

### Exploring Primer
- only affects Exploring XP
- out of scope for first-pass acquisition planning

### Energy Drink
- passive stamina refill over time
- out of scope for first-pass acquisition planning

---

## Apple Cider

### Base behavior
- without perks/upgrades, performs 1010 explores
- cannot be used unless player has at least 1010 stamina
- costs 40 apples to craft
- sets drop-rate behavior to 0.40 in every zone

### Cinnamon Sticks
- increases cider explores by 25%
- baseline rises from 1010 to 1263
- each EE point adds 12.5 explores instead of 10, rounded as needed

### Exploring Effectiveness (EE)
Without Cinnamon Sticks:
- effectively adds 10 explores per EE point

With Cinnamon Sticks:
- effectively adds 12.5 explores per EE point, rounded as needed

### Sprint Shoes
- increase effective EE
- should be modeled as transforming effective EE rather than as a separate yield multiplier

### Neigh
- reduces cider stamina cost by 20%
- stacks multiplicatively with Wanderer

### Cabbage Stew
- allows 5 ciders per click
- throughput/click effect only for now, not baseline efficiency math

### Cider optimization note
Cider should not be assumed globally optimal.
Its value depends on:
- zone
- perks
- meals
- Exploring Effectiveness
- opportunity cost of apples

---

## Lemonade

- normally gives 10 items instantly while exploring
- with Lemon Squeezer, gives 20
- gives Exploring XP when used, but XP is out of scope for first-pass planning
- should be treated as a fixed-yield exploring consumable
- does not interact with Exploring Effectiveness

---

## Arnold Palmer

- crafted from 1 Iced Tea + 20 Lemonade
- requires Crafting level 92
- normally gives 200 items
- with Lemon Squeezer, gives 500 items
- should be treated as both:
  - a direct source class when used
  - a crafted item with recipe/resource burden

### AP-related modifiers

#### Quandary Chowder
- +10% Lemonade/AP effectiveness
- user-toggleable
- quantity modifier, not mastery modifier

#### Lemon Seltzer
- +50% AP items for 50 uses
- action-limited, not time-limited
- stacks multiplicatively with Quandary Chowder
- first-pass planning should ignore bounded-use complications and treat this as out of scope or simplified

#### Lemon Cream Pie
- multi-use / throughput effect
- not baseline efficiency math in first pass

---

## Owned containers / stockpile conversion

Examples:
- corn prize bags
- owned chests

Properties:
- finite
- immediate
- should generally be modeled as “available now” sources
- should be separable from future acquisition

---

## Pets

### Core rules
- pets return 1 item per pet level per hour
- each pet can hold up to inventory max of each item it can gather
- pets stop producing after 48 hours offline

### Seasonal pets
- only produce during their active two-month period
- stored items remain collectible at any time
- future production depends on whether the pet is currently in season

### Special-case pets
Pet-specific exceptions should be represented as source-specific override rules in the source catalog.

Example:
- Owl at level 6+ gives double honey

### Pet modifiers
#### Crunchy Omelette
- 1.5x collected pet quantity
- quantity modifier

#### Mushroom Stew
- applies to mastery gained from pet collection
- mastery modifier

### Planning direction
- support stored pet inventory
- support simple future pet production estimates, reported separately
- pet inventory should ideally be entered via manual import parser, not only item-by-item manual entry

